 **Creation** — delivery docs are born in `Stories/<TICKET>/` as working drafts. No doc goes directly to HLD, LLD, or the Engineering Guide without passing through a ticket.
 
-**Graduation** — content graduates at two points: during `/dev document` (implementation outcomes) and during `/design publish` (design outcomes). Only settled outcomes graduate — rationale, comparisons, and open questions stay in the Story. Where an implementation change lands (HLD vs LLD) is determined by the HLD/LLD placement matrix in `dev/references/06-document.md`: HLD hit → update the relevant HLD doc and record detail in the LLD; HLD miss → create a minimal new HLD entry and capture full detail in the LLD. Design graduation is track-routed, resolved once in Frame and recorded in `Report.md`'s `## Context` section: Product lands in `{{PRODUCT_CONTEXT_DIR}}/`; Project lands in `Target Architecture (HLD)/`.
